cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this question set or these results, please cite them as below. A versioned DOI is minted for each GitHub release through Zenodo; the concept DOI is added here once the first release is archived."
type: dataset
title: "freightutils-eval: frontier language models on 300 freight reference questions — alone, with the FreightUtils tools, and with web search"
authors:
  - family-names: Cristoiu
    given-names: Marius
    affiliation: FreightUtils
repository-code: "https://github.com/SoapyRED/freightutils-eval"
url: "https://www.freightutils.com/eval"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
abstract: "A reproducible measurement of how often frontier language models answer freight reference questions correctly on their own, with the FreightUtils tools (MCP and REST), and with a provider's web search in place of the tools. 300 questions in six families, each with one expected value and a deterministic string scorer; the frozen question set, the harness, the scoring rule and every run's per-question answers, summary figures and spend are in the archive. The question set is CC BY 4.0; the harness and scripts are MIT."
keywords:
  - freight
  - dangerous goods
  - ADR
  - ADR 2027
  - HS codes
  - UN/LOCODE
  - air cargo
  - LLM evaluation
  - benchmark
  - tool use
  - Model Context Protocol
  - web search
